  "security_implications": "last_working_st stores the previous working state of the key manager. If corrupted by a sampling glitch or left stale (update_en low for long periods), the stored state may not reflect the actual operational condition. This could allow secret-key operations in an unauthorized state, leading to key exposure or misuse. Additionally, the reset value StReset must be a strictly restricted state; any oversight could permit key access before secure initialization, constituting a severe security vulnerability.",
